  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 510.10 Registration Listing Access",
  "priorExpiration": "2012-03-15",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 510.10 Registration Listing Access.\n\n(a) For the purposes of this section, \"registration listing\" means the name, address, and date of birth of the registrant, and if requested, the New Hampshire registration plate number and a description of the vehicle.\n\n(b) All requests for registration listings shall be processed in accordance with the requirements of RSA 260:14 and Saf-C 5600.\n\n(c) Registration listings that conform with the requirements of (b) above, shall be furnished for a fee of $5 per listing pursuant to RSA 261:60, I.\n\n(d) No registration listing shall be furnished in the case of permanent unlisted plates issued to a law enforcement agency.\n\nSource. #7972, eff 10-17-03 (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Saf-C 500) ss by #9995, INTERIM, eff 9-17-11, EXPIRED: 3-15-12\n\nNew. #10135, eff 5-23-12; ss by #13521, eff 1-13-23 (formerly Saf-C 510.10)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c500.html"
